---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/post.css';
---

<Base title="Terms & Conditions | Opera Shalem" description="Terms governing use of the Opera Shalem website.">
  <main>
    <article class="blog-post-page">
      <header class="post-header">
        <h1 class="post-title">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span class="post-date">Last updated: 2 November 2026</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="post-content">
        <p>These terms govern your use of the Opera Shalem website (operashalem.com). By using the site, you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>

        <h2>1. About Opera Shalem</h2>

        <p>Opera Shalem is a cultural initiative in formation, based in Jerusalem, Israel, working towards establishing a permanent ensemble opera institution. It has not yet been incorporated as a legal entity. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:info@operashalem.com">info@operashalem.com</a>.</p>

        <h2>2. Plans and figures are forward-looking</h2>

        <p>This website describes plans, phases, budgets, timelines, and goals that have not yet been achieved. They reflect our current intentions and estimates and may change. Nothing on this site is a promise that any plan will be carried out as described.</p>

        <p>Nothing on this site is an offer of securities or of any financial investment, a solicitation of donations, or tax advice. Any support, partnership, or funding arrangement will be agreed separately and in writing.</p>

        <h2>3. Information on this site</h2>

        <p>We aim to keep the content accurate and up to date, but we provide it for general information only and make no warranties about its completeness or accuracy. Blog posts reflect the views of their authors at the time of writing.</p>

        <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>

        <p>The Opera Shalem name and logo, and the text, design, and other content of this site, belong to Opera Shalem or are used with permission. You may share links to our pages and quote short extracts from our blog with attribution and a link to the original. Any other reproduction or use requires our written permission.</p>

        <h2>5. Links to other websites</h2>

        <p>Our pages link to external websites for reference. We are not responsible for their content, availability, or privacy practices, and a link does not imply endorsement.</p>

        <h2>6. Using the contact form</h2>

        <p>Please use the contact form only for genuine enquiries. Do not send unlawful, abusive, or misleading content, or material that infringes anyone's rights. How we handle the details you send is described in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

        <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>

        <p>The site is provided "as is". To the fullest extent permitted by law, Opera Shalem is not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of, or reliance on, the site or its content. Nothing in these terms limits any liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>

        <h2>8. Governing law</h2>

        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Israel. The competent courts in Jerusalem have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them, except where the law of your country of residence gives you the right to bring proceedings locally.</p>

        <h2>9. Changes</h2>

        <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of the page shows when they were last revised.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .post-content :global(ul) {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .post-content :global(li) {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
